.TH AVR\-GROUP\-EDIT 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-group-edit \- Rename a group or change its label.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr group edit
[OPTIONS] GROUP
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rename a group or change its label.
.PP
GROUP is a group ID (grp-...), the group's path from the root group, such as Organization/Platform/CI, or the end of a path when only one group has it, such as Platform/CI.
.PP
Only the options you pass change; --label '' clears the label.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr group edit Platform/CI --name Builds
    avr group edit Platform/CI --label ''
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    created_at, display_name, group_id, label, member_count, ownership,
    parent_id, soft_deleted_at, state, suspension_reason, updated_at
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIGROUP\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fITEXT\fR
The group's new name.
.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR \fITEXT\fR
The group's new label; an empty value clears it.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
